<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Feb 22.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Feb 22.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to Feb 22 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week Feb 16-Feb 22</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,869,129 tns	211,025 tns    11.29 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,888,197 tns	207,484 tns    10.99 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,756,410 tns	193,534 tns    11.02 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to Feb 22</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    18,201,191 tns    1,912,674 tns    10.51 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    17,479,062 tns    1,796,274 tns    10.28 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    16,735,258 tns    1,710,983 tns    10.22 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 59 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 59 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 58 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9530</p>
</text>
